WEBVTT

00:00.100 --> 00:03.070
<b>3 Years Earlier</b>

00:03.870 --> 00:06.070
Lady Elfaria is amazing!

00:06.070 --> 00:08.360
So this is real rain!

00:08.360 --> 00:11.050
It's the first time I've ever seen it!

00:11.050 --> 00:13.830
The Magia Vander can even control the sky!

00:18.390 --> 00:21.560
It's so far... so incredibly far away.

00:23.150 --> 00:28.970
I want to stand by your side, but I can't 
control even a single drop of water.

00:31.420 --> 00:32.910
Elfie...

00:32.910 --> 00:35.970
Will I be able to catch up to you?

00:40.650 --> 00:42.920
You're gonna catch a cold.

00:51.110 --> 00:53.310
This is called an umbrella.

00:53.310 --> 00:55.190
I made it myself.

00:55.190 --> 00:57.500
I want to become an artificer, you see.

00:58.180 --> 00:59.500
Who are you?

00:59.810 --> 01:03.210
I'm Rosty. Rosty Nowman.

01:03.210 --> 01:05.880
As of today, I'm your roommate.

01:06.860 --> 01:11.100
I'd like to be your friend, Will Serfort.

01:20.120 --> 01:21.250
Rosty...

01:30.670 --> 01:34.780
You seem to have mastered the use 
of the Mage Queen's legacy, Caldron.

01:35.140 --> 01:39.030
I'm the one who kept him here 
at the academy.

01:39.030 --> 01:41.790
I have a duty to guide and support him.

01:42.550 --> 01:45.040
Editing his memories 
is progressing smoothly.

01:45.040 --> 01:48.550
This way, he can return 
to being his usual self.

01:48.550 --> 01:54.690
In exchange, his beloved Sleeping Beauty 
remains rocking in a cradle of memories.

01:55.710 --> 01:59.430
I wonder what you're 
dreaming of right now.

02:16.990 --> 02:21.700
Episode 17
The Day of Departure

03:34.960 --> 03:37.990
Oh! You're finally awake!

03:39.190 --> 03:41.870
Clairie... Ed...

03:42.150 --> 03:44.610
Regarding your own wounds
as a secondary priority...

03:44.610 --> 03:48.310
You haven't changed at all since 
our school days, you colossal idiot.

03:48.310 --> 03:52.950
Even if they won't kill you, you should
 still value your life a little more.

03:52.950 --> 03:53.910
Where are we?

03:53.910 --> 03:55.510
The school infirmary.

03:55.940 --> 03:57.020
Eliza.

03:57.530 --> 04:01.440
You collapsed on the academy roof
 last night, so I brought you here.

04:03.810 --> 04:06.850
I'm glad you woke up, Workner.

04:09.530 --> 04:13.980
Why are you acting like you're the lawful 
wife here, my dear vampire underclassman?

04:13.980 --> 04:16.390
Ah, my idiot witch senior.

04:16.390 --> 04:19.260
I'd say you're the one who 
should quit brazenly two-timing.

04:19.260 --> 04:21.990
Misunderstandings can do great harm
 and are painful to watch.

04:21.990 --> 04:26.140
I'm bound to Workner and Ed 
by passionate bonds of friendship!

04:26.140 --> 04:29.710
Stop trying to weasel your way between 
classmates, you thieving wench!

04:31.500 --> 04:33.750
Where's Will? What happened to him?

04:34.490 --> 04:36.700
Stop thrashing around, you fool.

04:36.700 --> 04:39.740
Headmistress Caldron is looking after him.

04:39.740 --> 04:40.760
The headmistress?

04:41.040 --> 04:44.810
Entrust things to that witch and
 they'll never turn out badly.

04:47.270 --> 04:49.670
For now, just be good and sleep.

04:54.270 --> 04:55.650
Everyone!

04:55.650 --> 04:58.900
I heard Professor Workner 
is all right! And so is he!

04:58.900 --> 05:00.780
Is that true, Lyril?

05:00.780 --> 05:04.010
Yeah, Professor Eliza told me.

05:04.010 --> 05:04.850
Will...

05:06.030 --> 05:10.040
The book-learner should be able
 to make an appearance at graduation.

05:10.040 --> 05:11.920
I'm so glad!

05:11.920 --> 05:14.090
He worked the hardest 
out of anyone, right?

05:13.130 --> 05:15.610
If he hadn't made it,
 that would sour everything.

05:15.610 --> 05:18.000
The guy's as tough as a dwarf.

05:16.670 --> 05:18.670
Naive, the lot of you.

05:19.610 --> 05:21.180
Julius?

05:21.180 --> 05:24.760
He has that incomprehensible 
power at his disposal.

05:24.760 --> 05:26.840
There was never a need to worry about him.

05:26.840 --> 05:29.410
Why would you say something 
so spiteful, Julius?

05:29.410 --> 05:30.290
The old you was—

05:30.290 --> 05:33.380
I'll thank you not to use 
the old me as a reference, Emma!

05:33.380 --> 05:37.690
Besides, not long ago, all of you scorned 
the laggard yourselves, didn't you?

05:38.830 --> 05:41.950
You're the ones pulling a convenient 
about-face, aren't you?

05:42.330 --> 05:46.450
The whole lot of you have been corrupted,
 just like my lord elf and...

05:46.790 --> 05:50.660
It appears to me that you're 
the one being obstinate here.

05:50.660 --> 05:53.040
Resorting to peer pressure, are we?

05:53.040 --> 05:55.420
I'd never give in to something like that.

05:55.700 --> 05:57.420
Even if you don't acknowledge him,

05:57.420 --> 06:00.670
you ought to feel a secret gratitude
in your heart for his saving you.

06:03.930 --> 06:09.200
Or have you forgotten a mage's 
noblesse oblige, good sir?

06:10.680 --> 06:14.690
Whatever the case, 
he can't ascend to the tower.

06:14.690 --> 06:16.040
It'll be such a relief!

06:18.200 --> 06:19.940
Sion, what do you think?

06:21.920 --> 06:23.010
Sion?

06:24.510 --> 06:28.260
The losses suffered at Terminalia include
roughly three thousand killed or wounded.

06:28.260 --> 06:31.700
The whereabouts of the leaders
 behind the attack are still unknown.

06:31.950 --> 06:35.060
Divide the investigation 
between the factions.

06:35.060 --> 06:38.320
For now, prioritize repairs in the capital.

06:38.320 --> 06:40.540
Understood, Lord Aaron.

06:40.540 --> 06:41.960
Also...

06:42.240 --> 06:44.340
Will Serfort.

06:45.920 --> 06:48.580
He has been a student at the academy.

06:48.580 --> 06:52.880
Why were we unable to ascertain 
his presence these past six years?

06:52.880 --> 06:55.400
Likely Headmistress Caldron's work.

06:55.400 --> 06:59.110
I believe she was concealing him 
until he fully matured.

06:59.110 --> 07:02.130
That cauldron witch...

07:02.130 --> 07:05.860
Logwell is one thing, but she makes 
too many decisions without consultation.

07:06.350 --> 07:11.120
From this point forward, supervision 
of the sword will be entrusted to Finn.

07:13.870 --> 07:18.130
Lord Aaron, what are your thoughts 
regarding Will Serfort?

07:19.210 --> 07:21.130
It is what it is.

07:21.710 --> 07:25.600
If this is the wand and sword 
of the Mage Queen's vow,

07:25.600 --> 07:27.630
then all will intersect one day.

07:30.260 --> 07:32.640
Pardon my tardiness, my king.

07:33.260 --> 07:36.180
Summoning us again after yesterday?

07:36.180 --> 07:38.400
Will this be another boring 
evaluation meeting?

07:39.110 --> 07:40.820
Cease your yammering, barbarian.

07:40.820 --> 07:42.900
Your voice pains my ears.

07:44.510 --> 07:47.400
We will share intelligence
concerning the attackers.

07:47.700 --> 07:51.410
Continue to dig up information 
on the all-student praxis incident.

07:51.410 --> 07:56.570
The capital, the dungeon, even inside the 
tower itself... Be exhaustively thorough.

07:57.320 --> 08:01.010
Have the recovered mage slayers
 yielded any clues?

08:01.010 --> 08:01.790
Nothing.

08:02.060 --> 08:04.140
What about the monsters?

08:04.140 --> 08:07.560
The Upper Institute's been rummaging 
through the carcasses, right?

08:07.560 --> 08:08.300
Nothing.

08:08.700 --> 08:11.800
Then you don't know anything, 
you incompetent king.

08:12.110 --> 08:14.310
Do you not have even an inkling?

08:14.740 --> 08:16.560
If I had to say...

08:16.980 --> 08:19.020
The great battle of ten years ago.

08:19.020 --> 08:24.440
This felt the same as those destroyers
who once shook the magical world.

08:25.650 --> 08:29.200
The Day of Near Doom... 
You think there were survivors?

08:29.530 --> 08:34.200
Sounds like fun! You think those filthy 
ghosts are coming back for more?

08:34.570 --> 08:36.500
And what of the possibility
 you're mistaken?

08:36.500 --> 08:40.210
Lefiya and my people made great sacrifices
to be rid of them completely.

08:40.830 --> 08:42.650
You scared?

08:42.650 --> 08:46.090
Oh, right. You didn't take part 
in that battle, did you?

08:46.350 --> 08:50.120
You gonna go running back 
to your forest, ladybug?

08:59.970 --> 09:03.940
This is why I never want to participate 
in the Magia Vander meetings.

09:03.940 --> 09:06.490
Have you a death wish, you wretched lout?

09:06.490 --> 09:09.440
Not the best line 
<i>after</i> you try to kill someone.

09:09.730 --> 09:13.700
How about I beat you 
to a pulp first? Well?!

09:13.700 --> 09:14.950
Stop it.

09:15.910 --> 09:19.070
Each faction will continue 
the investigation.

09:19.070 --> 09:23.210
The pruning of new buds, 
the Bloom, is nearly upon us.

09:23.490 --> 09:25.940
Do not neglect your preparations for that.

09:26.640 --> 09:28.060
Now then, Sarissa...

09:28.060 --> 09:28.970
Yes?!

09:28.970 --> 09:30.970
What are you doing over there?

09:30.970 --> 09:32.970
That would be, um...

09:33.230 --> 09:35.260
Where is that woman?

09:35.260 --> 09:38.110
All of the Magia Vander, 
without exception, were summoned.

09:38.910 --> 09:43.480
Well... she said she has a stomachache,
 so she won't be coming today.

10:04.090 --> 10:05.180
Colette.

10:07.250 --> 10:08.630
Lihanna.

10:08.630 --> 10:10.280
What are those flowers for?

10:11.050 --> 10:12.630
They're for Rosty.

10:13.470 --> 10:17.810
He doesn't have a grave yet, 
but I figured this is the least I can do.

10:20.160 --> 10:24.160
What was Rosty Nowman like?

10:24.160 --> 10:27.070
In truth, I don't really know myself.

10:27.070 --> 10:31.870
He was majoring in artificer studies, 
so I didn't see him much on campus.

10:32.470 --> 10:36.660
I heard he was a transfer student 
from the western capital of Terralis.

10:37.020 --> 10:42.410
He appeared suddenly, and just as
suddenly, he was glued to Will at the hip.

10:43.350 --> 10:46.230
I was jealous of him.

10:58.200 --> 11:02.310
But Will said that he'd made
 such a good friend...

11:02.310 --> 11:04.610
He seemed so happy.

11:06.140 --> 11:07.440
<b>Nightsblood Wand</b>

11:07.560 --> 11:10.940
<b><u>Eliza Nosferat</u>

Race: Rhizanth   Age: 25   Height: 169 cm
Birthday: 11th of Ahzomoon
Likes: Devil's cake, sugar in general, a relaxing coffee
Dislikes: Night, blood, lunatice (mock moons)
First Love: Workner Norgram

Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached: 31st
Equipment: Nightsblood wand
Skills: Nosefer Sique; all dark magic</b>

11:07.560 --> 11:10.940
<b>A professor at the academy who was one year 
below Workner and the others. Her skills place her 
in the top ranks of even the academy's fighting forces. 
As a pure insomniac, her self-depreciating jokes about
 the big dark circles under her eyes basically never fail. 
For example: "My makeup looks amazing today, no?"

When she was a student, she caused a certain incident that Workner personally resolved.
Ever since, she has been obsessed with him, followed him, and become a teacher at the academy.
She and Clairie fight like cats and dogs.</b>

11:11.150 --> 11:12.530
<b>Crimsonblue Wand</b>

11:11.150 --> 11:12.650
<b>Baja Broom</b>

11:12.570 --> 11:15.950
<b><u>Clairie Serah</u>

Race: Rhizanth   Age: 26   Height: 162 cm
Birthday: 20th of Roemoon
Likes: Workner, Edward, Caldron,
Caldron's homemade pot au feu
Dislikes: Eliza Nosferat
First Love: Golbathos, who lived 
in her neighborhood when she was little

Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached: 35th
Equipment: Crimsonblue wand, Baja broom
Skills: All fire and water magic; intermediate wind magic;
 cauldron magic learned directly from Caldron</b>

11:12.570 --> 11:15.950
<b>She is a multos who can use three types of magic 
and an arbiter who is not affiliated with any particular
 faction. When she was a student, she was part of a trio
with Workner and Edward—a squad of problem children.
Even now, when she can find the time, she forcibly drags 
the two of them to taverns where she babbles drunkenly. 
She says that one day, she'll have to settle things with
 her dear vampire underclassman.</b>

11:19.320 --> 11:21.390
Put it down here!

11:21.390 --> 11:22.750
Oh, sorry about that.

11:22.750 --> 11:24.330
That's Rigarden for you.

11:24.680 --> 11:28.400
With the help of the dwarves,
repairs are speeding right along.

11:31.790 --> 11:35.460
At this rate, things will soon look
 as they did before.

11:36.510 --> 11:37.430
Invess.

11:44.160 --> 11:45.430
Hey there, Iris.

11:46.070 --> 11:49.020
But I have asked you to stop 
calling me that, haven't I?

11:49.020 --> 11:51.100
I don't like that name.

11:51.100 --> 11:52.940
Then it's perfect, isn't it?

11:53.610 --> 11:56.950
After all, I despise you.

11:56.950 --> 11:59.720
I see you haven't changed.

11:59.720 --> 12:03.200
So, why call out to stop someone
you hate so very much?

12:05.320 --> 12:08.290
Please don't interfere with Will.

12:08.290 --> 12:12.250
If you get involved, the hands 
of the clock will advance all at once.

12:13.650 --> 12:17.920
And if that happens, there will be 
no stopping <i>that person</i> any longer.

12:18.390 --> 12:19.920
Color me surprised.

12:19.920 --> 12:22.810
I never imagined a watcher like you
 saying something like that.

12:23.390 --> 12:24.940
Do you have a thing for him?

12:24.940 --> 12:26.080
Who could possibly—

12:27.860 --> 12:30.560
Iris, I'm sorry to say...

12:31.110 --> 12:32.790
I will be taking him.

12:38.730 --> 12:40.710
Today is the graduation ceremony.

12:41.410 --> 12:44.560
Caldron's little games are over now.

12:46.540 --> 12:51.170
<b>1 Year Earlier</b>

12:46.840 --> 12:48.380
Hey, Will?

12:48.380 --> 12:52.400
Suppose... Just suppose
I wasn't around anymore.

12:53.300 --> 12:55.590
Would you be sad?

12:55.590 --> 12:57.800
What? What do you mean?

12:58.390 --> 13:03.020
After meeting you here and making 
so many more precious memories...

13:03.020 --> 13:05.060
I've started wondering.

13:05.330 --> 13:10.060
If I have to say goodbye 
and that saddens you...

13:10.060 --> 13:13.810
then maybe I never should have 
appeared before you in the first place.

13:13.810 --> 13:15.570
Th-That's not true at all!

13:15.890 --> 13:18.140
Rosty, I'm glad I met you!

13:18.140 --> 13:20.260
It's made me really happy!

13:20.260 --> 13:21.330
So...

13:21.760 --> 13:24.820
please don't say such sad things.

13:25.630 --> 13:27.050
I'm sorry.

13:27.050 --> 13:32.330
But, Will, when you ascend the tower,
I may not be by your side.

13:33.120 --> 13:35.670
You mean you won't have enough credits?

13:35.670 --> 13:37.950
Yeah, something like that.

13:39.340 --> 13:44.350
The day may come that I make Will Serfort,
 tower ascendant, very sad.

13:44.950 --> 13:45.850
But...

13:50.130 --> 13:52.070
I'll always be watching over you.

14:20.590 --> 14:23.800
My hair is... back to its normal color.

14:24.960 --> 14:27.120
I wonder what all of that was.

14:50.090 --> 14:54.580
If you were here, I wonder 
what you'd have to say to me.

14:55.180 --> 14:56.160
Rosty...

15:04.140 --> 15:05.470
I'm going now.

15:11.770 --> 15:15.770
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy 
Auditorium</b>

15:14.190 --> 15:17.030
Magical Doctrine Number 1.

15:17.950 --> 15:23.700
The great Mage Queen declared: 
"You may laugh. You may rejoice."

15:24.320 --> 15:28.820
"For whether they open or not, 
when the buds turn toward the sky,"

15:29.170 --> 15:31.460
"flowers shall surely dwell
in the heavens."

15:34.630 --> 15:39.580
In the Terminalia tragedy, 
many lives were lost.

15:40.150 --> 15:45.230
Teachers from our academy 
and no small number of our students.

15:45.940 --> 15:48.120
Along with high mages from the tower,

15:48.120 --> 15:51.170
they put their lives on the line 
to protect the people.

15:51.170 --> 15:55.100
To them, we offer our condolences
 and deepest respect.

15:55.570 --> 16:00.610
At the same time, we must
 put an end to hanging our heads.

16:00.910 --> 16:05.610
With the tower now under threat,
this tragedy was not a finale,

16:05.900 --> 16:10.120
but a warning bell signaling 
the beginning of calamity.

16:10.610 --> 16:16.120
It is our responsibility to carry the hope
we've nurtured into the future.

16:16.540 --> 16:22.250
Now, let us begin the Rigarden 
Magical Academy graduation ceremony.

16:24.550 --> 16:27.260
Rise, students of the 401st class.

16:28.260 --> 16:30.010
Line up in front of the stage.

16:30.010 --> 16:34.180
Those graduates whose names are called, 
stand ready to accept your certificates.

16:40.580 --> 16:42.020
Agnes Fouques.

16:43.770 --> 16:45.280
Ardens Rich.

16:46.530 --> 16:48.030
Austin Lott.

16:50.560 --> 16:52.190
Will Serfort.

16:53.500 --> 16:55.080
Valerie Rice.

16:56.310 --> 16:57.880
Zara Albrand.

16:59.040 --> 17:00.840
Zera Albrand.

17:02.110 --> 17:03.830
Zoe Garniga.

17:06.800 --> 17:09.500
That is all 250 names.

17:09.500 --> 17:13.110
These students have completed the
 required coursework at our academy,

17:13.110 --> 17:15.310
and we approve their graduation.

17:19.870 --> 17:21.810
And now, to conclude,

17:21.810 --> 17:24.560
I will announce those 
ascending to the tower.

17:25.060 --> 17:27.820
Those whose names are called, 
come up to the stage.

17:28.410 --> 17:34.320
You will be granted a Hat of Mercedes 
and the right to enter the tower.

17:34.780 --> 17:36.580
First, our valedictorian.

17:36.830 --> 17:39.420
Lihanna Owenzaus.

17:36.830 --> 17:40.540
<b>Lihanna Owenzaus
Total Credits: 12,000</b>

17:51.630 --> 17:53.090
Next, by rank...

17:53.090 --> 17:55.610
Wignall Lindor.

17:53.130 --> 17:56.350
<b>Wignall Lindor
Total Credits: 11,989</b>

17:56.350 --> 17:58.880
Juilus Reinberg.

17:56.430 --> 17:59.600
<b>Julius Reinberg
Total Credits: 11,802</b>

17:59.600 --> 18:01.920
Sion Ulster.

17:59.640 --> 18:02.850
<b>Sion Ulster
Total Credits: 11,801</b>

18:02.890 --> 18:05.610
<b>Emma Klever
Total Credits: 10,000</b>

18:03.150 --> 18:05.000
Emma Klever.

18:05.610 --> 18:07.890
Renaisse Arette.

18:05.650 --> 18:08.360
<b>Renaisee Arette
Total Credits: 9,655</b>

18:08.360 --> 18:10.630
Colette Loire.

18:08.420 --> 18:11.880
<b>Colette Loire
Total Credits: 9,024</b>

18:11.480 --> 18:13.430
Rose Prehnite.

18:14.360 --> 18:16.230
Jorua Moraine.

18:17.180 --> 18:18.970
Gordon Vally.

18:19.870 --> 18:21.400
Lyril...

18:23.100 --> 18:27.190
These 49 have obtained 
the necessary credits

18:27.190 --> 18:29.380
and will advance to the tower.

18:33.810 --> 18:35.960
<i>I'm sorry, Elfie.</i>

18:36.640 --> 18:39.390
However, there is one more student.

18:39.780 --> 18:44.150
One who was deemed to advance
right at the very last moment.

18:48.270 --> 18:51.400
There are two conditions for advancing.

18:51.400 --> 18:55.030
The first is to earn
 7,200 credits or more.

18:55.030 --> 18:59.280
The other is to create a new spell.

18:59.700 --> 19:03.900
The spell in question cleansed
 all of us of our despair.

19:03.900 --> 19:08.430
It protected countless lives 
and saved the capital.

19:09.290 --> 19:14.360
It is a splendid accomplishment, 
a great feat worthy of praise.

19:15.020 --> 19:16.680
And the name of that spell is...

19:17.750 --> 19:19.050
"Courage"!

19:21.910 --> 19:23.680
Will Serfort.

19:24.170 --> 19:25.240
Come forward.

19:26.190 --> 19:27.060
Headmistress!

19:28.500 --> 19:30.980
There are certainly those 
who disagree with this!

19:31.230 --> 19:35.740
But for those who acknowledge
 his courage as magic...

19:35.740 --> 19:38.150
give a round of applause!

20:31.710 --> 20:33.100
Ed.

20:33.100 --> 20:34.220
That's enough, isn't it?

20:34.220 --> 20:36.150
No, absolutely not!

20:36.150 --> 20:40.310
How can you tease such a sweet dream only
to shove him into the pits of despair?

20:40.740 --> 20:44.520
Why does he have to suffer 
the same fate I did?

20:45.520 --> 20:47.360
I'm sure he'll overcome it.

20:47.770 --> 20:51.820
After all, he's been thoroughly trained 
by a very scary, very kind teacher.

20:56.120 --> 20:58.140
You're a greedy one, Caldron.

20:58.640 --> 21:03.080
I suppose I'll spur the sword on and
 go looking for some new vistas.

21:03.080 --> 21:05.120
Now, I present these fifty students.

21:05.420 --> 21:11.370
By the will of all gathered here, they are
hereby approved to ascend to the tower.

21:11.860 --> 21:14.610
You are the Grim Generation.

21:14.610 --> 21:20.190
Ahead of you, trouble no doubt lies
 in wait. You will face many a trial.

21:20.640 --> 21:26.390
But even so, you must find your place 
in the heavens and drive off evil!

21:31.790 --> 21:34.000
Congratulations, Will.

21:35.810 --> 21:38.400
It seems the academy 
ceremony has concluded.

21:38.710 --> 21:41.400
Now, new mages will come 
to the tower and...

21:42.710 --> 21:44.040
Lady Elfaria?

21:45.330 --> 21:47.460
I've been waiting for you, Will.

21:49.410 --> 21:51.790
<i>Year 504 of the Magical Era.</i>

